Want to view your timetable, check your grades or register for an exam? You can do this with the MyInholland-app. This app is intended for current students of Inholland University of Applied Sciences.



What can you do with the MyInholland app?

With the MyInholland-app you can: 

- view your own timetable;

- easily keep track of your grades;

- register or deregister for exams;

- receive a notification when something changes in your timetable;

- view the timetables of lecturers and courses;

- check the availability of classrooms and project rooms.

 

Are you a prospective student looking for information about introduction day(s)? Then download the Inholland MyStart-app. With this app, you can also check the status of your enrolment and view the list of books and other study materials.

The MyESL-app is the app for students of Erasmus School of Law. Via the app you have access to your timetable, you receive important announcements and you can easily find out who to contact for a specific question. The app is specially designed to optimise your study convenience.

With the MyESL-app you can:

• View your timetable;
• View your results;
• Look up useful information;
• View contact details;
• View the campus map.

The Albeda app is the official app for all students at Albeda! In the app you will find information that is important to you as a student. Everything at hand, via your smartphone!

What does the Albeda app offer?
- Your timetable and changes to the timetable;
- Your results;
- The latest Albeda news;
- Your attendance and absence;
- Handy (general) information.

Language learning app LinGo Play is an interesting and effective vocabulary trainer to learn words and phrases through flashcards and online games. Download the language learning app LinGo Play and try it!

The LinGo language course includes the following topics: Education, Business, People, Home, Nature, Animals, Science, Sports and Tourism, Art, Food, Appliances, Furniture, Beauty and Health, Medicine, as well as many other topics…

Learn foreign language through LinGo’s many features:
‣ 5172 flashcards, 4141 words, 373 phrases;
‣ 600+ English lessons;
‣ 16 exercises;
‣ English course for beginners;
‣ Advanced content for linguists and native speakers;
‣ Tests and grades;
‣ Single player;
‣ Online multiplayer;
